                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a165fdb1-5174-32a7-b4d9-eb557dd0674e",
                        "entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Neigung zu ausgefallenen, absurd-komischen Ideen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "unzählbar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "455efaea-6e27-4972-a86d-48641e3744fa",
                                "sense_id": "a165fdb1-5174-32a7-b4d9-eb557dd0674e",
                                "text": "Ihm war nicht ganz klar, ob seine Skurrilität die Kollegen mehr belustigte oder nervte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "289965eb-8674-4508-bcb9-561bd1b6cb2a",
                                "sense_id": "a165fdb1-5174-32a7-b4d9-eb557dd0674e",
                                "text": "„Wichtiger aber als solche Skurrilitäten ist, dass Rousseau sich seinen Menschen im Naturzustand als Einzelgänger denkt.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e7f9741-35bd-3a87-9961-310c21295a9e",
                        "entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ausgefallene, absurd-komische Idee"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "zählbar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "54e5ea26-3f3d-4550-a36a-f79bbf5859a6",
                                "sense_id": "9e7f9741-35bd-3a87-9961-310c21295a9e",
                                "text": "Und sie hatte noch mehr solcher Skurrilitäten auf Lager!"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e54f9f16-266d-483d-b2e8-8b35d8a9c8e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "source_sense_id": "a165fdb1-5174-32a7-b4d9-eb557dd0674e",
                        "source_sense_description": "unzählbar: Neigung zu ausgefallenen, absurd-komischen Ideen",
                        "target_lang_word": "bizarrerie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bizarrerie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère de ce qui est bizarre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "deb39877-cf22-4c0b-8573-e84230cc7f5d",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Cette bizarrerie même de m'avoir envoyé une jolie fille pour me consoler, j'aurais parié qu'elle venait de son invention, et que c'était un effet de sa compassion pour mes peines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3173faf-709a-486c-8ac5-f09319c678cf",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Gardez-vous donc bien d’imiter le vulgaire, qui met la Fortune au nombre des dieux ; la bizarrerie de sa conduite l’éloigne entièrement du caractère de la divinité […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff31e0c9-ed89-4d30-a12a-d2ab5c7a58da",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Petites plantes annuelles, herbacées, voisines des Luzernes (Medicago), que l’on sème sur place terreautée, et que l’on cultive pour la bizarrerie de leurs fruits, qui sont hérissés, écailleux, sillonnés, et imitent parfaitement une chenille, quelquefois un limaçon ou un ver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c933025-2905-470f-bd4c-546ebefd2b02",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "[…] et, par une bizarrerie quelquefois observée, le météore était paré de toutes les couleurs du prisme, entre lesquelles le rouge s’accusait plus nettement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chose bizarre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23b4b1b1-f342-4557-9344-967ee3fa5144",
                                                "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                                "text": "Beaucoup de ces tournures, et particulièrement les idiotismes de figures, constituent des bizarreries dans la langue même qui les a enfantées ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f33b2c-303e-423f-8bff-3cfb3abdcd10",
                                                "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                                "text": "La bizarrerie administrative dont elle est victime, Othe s'en accommode depuis fort longtemps. Pensez donc ! Depuis 1790 (création des départements) qu'elle vit avec son statut d'enclave meurthe-et-mosellane en territoire meusien, elle s’est fait une raison."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Humeur bizarre ; extravagance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28ebd02b-dc32-4ab1-987c-880aa061ac9d",
                                                "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                                "text": "Enfin, comme c’est un Anglais qui voyage, on doit s’attendre à des bizarreries, mais cela passe la permission."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea37faf4-0e70-4d56-90c9-ef352b6ac04b",
                                                "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                                "text": "Je n’ai jamais vraiment essayé de me débarrasser de ces bizarreries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b46b3b53-3bfd-4ad5-bf92-68295b488e46",
                        "source_entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e7f9741-35bd-3a87-9961-310c21295a9e",
                        "source_sense_description": "zählbar: ausgefallene, absurd-komische Idee",
                        "target_lang_word": "whimsy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whimsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                        "entry_id": "f71c9342-0d10-3c38-bd30-d5c7dd177ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A quaint and fanciful idea; a whim; playfully odd behaviour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b01ab8c-1284-4370-b631-9edc41c56ce7",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "[…] Take heed of filling their [i.e., children's] heads with VVhimzies, and unprofitable Notions; for this vvill ſooner learn them to be malepert and proud, than ſober and humble."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff26d9ef-b375-4fee-b9fe-0322cf99202f",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "These days! where e'en th' extravagance of poetry, / Is at a loss for figures to express / Men's folly, whimsies, and inconstancy, / And by a faint description makes them less."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9685058-bb1a-460e-a7b6-274bd15efedc",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "[A]ll the ridiculous and extravagant ſhapes that can be imagin'd, all the fancies and whimſies of Poets and Painters and Ægyptian Idolaters, if ſo be they are conſiſtent with Life and Propagation, would be now actually in Being, if our Atheiſt's Notion were true: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38714548-44ac-4470-9a06-1f7e7bb6a84f",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "Egad, if her Majeſty has often theſe VVhimſies, I ſhall petition the Court to build a Bridge over the River, or let me reſign my Employment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2a0d312-12c5-431e-8e31-703f1f92609e",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "It’s a lovely sequence cut too short because the show seems afraid to give itself over to romance and whimsy and wistfulness when it has wedgie jokes to deliver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b55b559-bb5e-40ad-a62a-9389bce79354",
                                                "sense_id": "df4e0c44-2321-3113-9a55-daaef08f48ac",
                                                "text": "[…] but in effect it seemed to have heaps of Amelie-style whimsy but no deeper unity or coherence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "028711ec-d30f-3f86-9986-7e7a92c0d992",
                                        "entry_id": "f71c9342-0d10-3c38-bd30-d5c7dd177ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An impulsive, illogical or capricious character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a1719d8-56cb-3d1b-aa3c-315577592da9",
                                        "entry_id": "f71c9342-0d10-3c38-bd30-d5c7dd177ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A whim (capstan or vertical drum)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2c015b2-102c-3bc3-ab6c-948624d41405",
                                        "entry_id": "f71c9342-0d10-3c38-bd30-d5c7dd177ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A jigsaw puzzle piece that has been cut into a recognizable shape, as if on a whim; often the shape is representative of the theme of the image used for the puzzle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb4b95ed-619e-4e3c-a182-9d529f79b339",
                                                "sense_id": "e2c015b2-102c-3bc3-ab6c-948624d41405",
                                                "text": "\"Dori, you have to solve this puzzle!\" / \"Sure, right away doctor. Quality construction … clean edges. Oh, a whimsy!\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6909daa7-effc-31ff-8a82-6d6f4c6e81f1",
                                        "entry_id": "f71c9342-0d10-3c38-bd30-d5c7dd177ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The support that protects a finished piece as it is detached from a punty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whimsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34feb34f-7d77-35ff-822d-2e81fa9da382",
                                        "entry_id": "790db5cd-eae4-3b22-8b15-a3ca08e61b80",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fill with whimsies or whims; to make fantastic; to craze."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3dacdc3-41b2-44fe-bafa-f686f7c4fef9",
                                                "sense_id": "34feb34f-7d77-35ff-822d-2e81fa9da382",
                                                "text": "A wantonneſſe in wealth, methinks I agree not with, / Tis ſuch a trouble to be married too, / And have a thouſand things of great importance, / Jewells and plates, and fooleries moleſt mee, / To have a mans brains whimſied with his wealth: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whimsy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "202f7ffa-2bb6-3a92-b147-47da5930b444",
                                        "entry_id": "819660bf-aaf0-3970-88d1-7bdec0d0eb16",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of whimsical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6b654c1-09ff-4dd9-9284-fceea366e42c",
                                                "sense_id": "202f7ffa-2bb6-3a92-b147-47da5930b444",
                                                "text": "Whimsiest of the fairy brood, I cannot scold you if I would"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f9e75a-ebc6-4817-82da-0706cf027775",
                                                "sense_id": "202f7ffa-2bb6-3a92-b147-47da5930b444",
                                                "text": "[…] and if in a whimsy mood I choose to read the opening chapters last, and the closing chapters first, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "33bf8181-2756-45da-b7d4-485cf0cf08cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e7f9741-35bd-3a87-9961-310c21295a9e",
                        "source_sense_description": "zählbar: ausgefallene, absurd-komische Idee",
                        "target_lang_word": "oddity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "oddity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An odd or strange thing or opinion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92e088b3-c714-43a6-9426-d063213a1f19",
                                                "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                                "text": "In the old days, to my commonplace and unobserving mind, he gave no evidences of genius whatsoever. He never read me any of his manuscripts, […], and therefore my lack of detection of his promise may in some degree be pardoned. But he had then none of the oddities and mannerisms which I hold to be inseparable from genius, and which struck my attention in after days when I came in contact with the Celebrity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccab287e-8a0c-41f3-af3b-1d2f74961972",
                                                "sense_id": "1746217a-7f58-3f33-9660-196818e1f4ac",
                                                "text": "An Avonside 0-4-4T with outside cylinders, bought by the S.M.A. in 1882 and scrapped in 1892 as a dismal failure, was one of the motive power oddities (some of them mortgaged)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "891a258e-a7c5-38ab-80d4-2f0e81bd26ea",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A strange person; an oddball."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6c3ac3b-bdba-4929-b562-9445cb90f14a",
                                                "sense_id": "891a258e-a7c5-38ab-80d4-2f0e81bd26ea",
                                                "text": "Fête succeeded fête in honour of the arrival of Christina of Sweden, who seemed to communicate her own reckless love of novelty to the then somewhat staid French court. Claim your privileges as an oddity, and even you yourself will be astonished at their extent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f79b181-a7fb-35cc-82fe-fdff1cee1541",
                                        "entry_id": "b39a8963-3ab5-312b-a1e4-ce52e0dd6057",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Strangeness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba090a78-d583-40a7-a6b6-b16c69b42be2",
                                                "sense_id": "4f79b181-a7fb-35cc-82fe-fdff1cee1541",
                                                "text": "The thing was unprecedented in his experience, and probably he wondered in his equine way at the eccentricities of the human race, and questioned whether oddity might not be merging into insanity in his master’s case."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bff47b7a-d094-4286-973b-1e10e2c351bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "8056980b-daaa-3b54-a6ea-ccc0e00c1631",
                        "source_sense_id": "9e7f9741-35bd-3a87-9961-310c21295a9e",
                        "source_sense_description": "zählbar: ausgefallene, absurd-komische Idee",
                        "target_lang_word": "bizarrerie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bizarrerie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère de ce qui est bizarre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "deb39877-cf22-4c0b-8573-e84230cc7f5d",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Cette bizarrerie même de m'avoir envoyé une jolie fille pour me consoler, j'aurais parié qu'elle venait de son invention, et que c'était un effet de sa compassion pour mes peines."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3173faf-709a-486c-8ac5-f09319c678cf",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Gardez-vous donc bien d’imiter le vulgaire, qui met la Fortune au nombre des dieux ; la bizarrerie de sa conduite l’éloigne entièrement du caractère de la divinité […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff31e0c9-ed89-4d30-a12a-d2ab5c7a58da",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "Petites plantes annuelles, herbacées, voisines des Luzernes (Medicago), que l’on sème sur place terreautée, et que l’on cultive pour la bizarrerie de leurs fruits, qui sont hérissés, écailleux, sillonnés, et imitent parfaitement une chenille, quelquefois un limaçon ou un ver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c933025-2905-470f-bd4c-546ebefd2b02",
                                                "sense_id": "aa3fd05f-b82a-3e66-b21d-d836903071cc",
                                                "text": "[…] et, par une bizarrerie quelquefois observée, le météore était paré de toutes les couleurs du prisme, entre lesquelles le rouge s’accusait plus nettement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chose bizarre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23b4b1b1-f342-4557-9344-967ee3fa5144",
                                                "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                                "text": "Beaucoup de ces tournures, et particulièrement les idiotismes de figures, constituent des bizarreries dans la langue même qui les a enfantées ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f33b2c-303e-423f-8bff-3cfb3abdcd10",
                                                "sense_id": "be83d175-ef31-337b-af2a-322247018319",
                                                "text": "La bizarrerie administrative dont elle est victime, Othe s'en accommode depuis fort longtemps. Pensez donc ! Depuis 1790 (création des départements) qu'elle vit avec son statut d'enclave meurthe-et-mosellane en territoire meusien, elle s’est fait une raison."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                        "entry_id": "f6e2c53a-e471-3011-bb0b-576b371b196c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Humeur bizarre ; extravagance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28ebd02b-dc32-4ab1-987c-880aa061ac9d",
                                                "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                                "text": "Enfin, comme c’est un Anglais qui voyage, on doit s’attendre à des bizarreries, mais cela passe la permission."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea37faf4-0e70-4d56-90c9-ef352b6ac04b",
                                                "sense_id": "46b1dfae-370d-3495-80c9-454a7d7bb5b1",
                                                "text": "Je n’ai jamais vraiment essayé de me débarrasser de ces bizarreries."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
